<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 26 June, from 1243 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1243">1243 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">783 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols crush the Seljuks of Rûm at Köse Dağ</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Mongol army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baiju">Baiju</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykhusraw-ii">Kaykhusraw II</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. The Seljuk sultanate became a Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and broke into the principalities from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> emerged.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George IV dies at Windsor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former Prince Regent, known for extravagance and his patronage of architecture, died at 67. His brother William IV succeeded him, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reform-act-1832">Great Reform Act</a> followed in 1832.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/queen-victoria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1857">1857 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">169 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria presents the first Victoria Crosses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Hyde Park, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> decorated 62 servicemen for valour in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a>. The Victoria Cross remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s highest award for gallantry.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United Nations Charter is signed in San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 50 nations signed the Charter creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> to maintain peace and security. It came into force in October 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy tells West Berlin 'Ich bin ein Berliner'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking at Rathaus Schöneberg to a crowd of about 450,000, President Kennedy declared solidarity with the people of the walled city two years after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> went up.</p></div></li></ol>
